  "name": "HD44780",
  "specs": {
    "characters": "16×2, 16×4, 20×4 (controller is the same)",
    "current": "1.5 mA logic + LED backlight (~20 mA per LED)",
    "interface": "4-bit or 8-bit parallel, or I²C via PCF8574 backpack",
    "voltage": "5V (logic — 3.3V works on some clones but contrast suffers)"
  },
  "tips": [
    "Most hobby modules ship with a PCF8574 I²C backpack — much fewer pins. The Volt 'lcd16x2' / 'lcd20x4' drivers wrap this.",
    "Always include the 10kΩ contrast pot — without it the display looks blank or has black blocks.",
    "Custom characters: 8 CGRAM slots, 5×8 pixels each."
  ],
